==Old Irish==

===Etymology===
{{unc|sga}}. Originally a neuter s-stem, perhaps {{m|cel-pro||*ugos}}. 

This word '''cannot''' be derived from {{noncog|cel-pro|*āwyom}} (from which Brittonic words {{noncog|cy|wy|t=egg}} descend), from {{noncog|ine-pro|*h₂ōwyóm}},<ref>{{R:cel:EDPC|page=50|head=*āwyo-}}</ref><ref>{{cite-journal|year=1969|author=Jochem Schindler|title=Die idg. Wörter 'Vogel' und 'Ei'|journal=Die Sprache|volume=15|page=162}}</ref> because the ''-g-'' and the vowel in Old Irish are unaccounted for.

